Based on the table above: 1 yard to go - Both teams go for it (run the ball) as their pass rates are quite low and matches what most teams in the NFL do
2 to 3 yards to go - Teams in the NFL are likely to pass as the average is close to 90%. Here, the Patriots are below the NFL average so can be expected to run the ball. For Rams, they most likely will pass when going for it, but for the first half the sample sizes for both teams is quite low.
